      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between Slavic hair and other types of human hair extensions?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The primary differences are in the hair's natural fineness, cuticle integrity, and structural compatibility with most Western hair types. Slavic hair is naturally fine in strand diameter, which allows it to blend with fine and medium hair textures in a way that coarser donor hair cannot. It is also remy, meaning the cuticle is intact, and all strands run in the same direction, which prevents tangling, preserves shine, and extends the life of the hair significantly. Hair marketed as Brazilian, Peruvian, or Indian is often thicker in strand diameter and may have had the cuticle stripped through acid processing, which gives it an initial softness that deteriorates quickly. Slavic hair maintains its quality from the first day of wear through multiple application cycles."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is all Slavic hair the same quality, or does it vary between suppliers?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It varies considerably, and this is one of the most important things to understand when evaluating hair extension salons. Not all hair labelled as Slavic or European is genuinely sourced from the region, and not all that is genuinely sourced is handled with the same care through processing and storage. At Luxe Aura Hair we source our hair specifically for its quality and consistency, and every batch meets the standards our team has established for cuticle integrity, colour consistency, and strand strength before it is used in any installation. The difference between premium and average Slavic hair is visible in the finished result and felt in how the hair behaves during wear."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can Slavic hair be coloured and highlighted after installation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, because it is 100% real human hair with an intact cuticle, it responds to professional colour, toning, and highlighting exactly as natural hair does. We recommend having any colour work done in the salon by our team rather than at home, both to ensure the most precise and seamless result and to protect the hair's quality through the colouring process. Many of our clients have balayage, highlights, or toning applied through their extensions at the same appointment as their installation or at a follow-up visit, creating a dimensional colour result that is completely unified from their natural roots through the extension lengths."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does Slavic human hair last with proper care?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "With proper care and regular maintenance appointments, the hair itself is reusable across multiple application cycles, meaning you are not purchasing new hair at every maintenance visit, only paying for the stylist's time and any supplemental strands needed to replace natural shedding. The lifespan of the hair depends on how well it is cared for at home, how frequently it is heat-styled, and whether it is washed with sulphate-free products as recommended. Clients who follow our aftercare guidance consistently find their Slavic hair remains in excellent condition for a year or more across repeated applications."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why do you carry over 80 colours in stock rather than ordering hair per client?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Carrying over 80 colours in stock at all times is a deliberate choice that serves our clients in two important ways. First, it means same-day installations are always possible, you never have to wait a week or two for your hair to arrive before your appointment can be scheduled. Second, and more importantly for quality, it means our stylists can assess your natural hair in person under real salon lighting and select the exact shade or combination of shades that creates the most seamless blend — rather than trying to guess your colour from a description or a photograph. Colour matching done in person with hair in hand is always more accurate than colour matching done remotely, and that accuracy is a significant part of what makes the final result look as natural as it does."
          }
        }
